---
// Static graphical method diagram for the worked example: the 2
// constraint lines, small arrows marking each half-space's feasible
// side, the shaded feasible region, and its 4 vertices.
import CartesianGraph from "./primitives/cartesian-graph.astro";
---

<CartesianGraph
  captionSlot
  title="Graphical Method Worked Example"
  desc="The feasible region of a two-variable linear program, bounded by two constraints and the axes. Arrows point to each constraint's feasible half-plane."
  y={{ label: "x₂", domain: [0, 5.4] }}
  x={{ label: "x₁", domain: [0, 6.8] }}
  areas={[
    {
      points: [
        { x: 0, y: 0 },
        { x: 4, y: 0 },
        { x: 3, y: 1 },
        { x: 0, y: 2 },
      ],
      tone: "s5",
      opacity: 0.15,
    },
  ]}
  curves={[
    {
      equation: (x1) => 4 - x1,
      domain: [0, 4],
      tone: "s5",
    },
    {
      equation: (x1) => (6 - x1) / 3,
      domain: [0, 6],
      tone: "ct",
    },
  ]}
  lines={[
    {
      from: { x: 2, y: 2 },
      to: { x: 1.74, y: 1.74 },
      tone: "s5",
      width: 1.5,
      arrow: "end",
    },
    {
      from: { x: 3, y: 1 },
      to: { x: 2.88, y: 0.66 },
      tone: "ct",
      width: 1.5,
      arrow: "end",
    },
  ]}
  points={[
    { x: 0, y: 0, tone: "ink" },
    { x: 4, y: 0, tone: "ink" },
    { x: 3, y: 1, tone: "pt", radius: 5.5 },
    { x: 0, y: 2, tone: "ink" },
  ]}
  labels={[
    { text: "x₁ + x₂ = 4", x: 2, y: 3.2, tone: "s5", weight: 600 },
    { text: "x₁ + 3x₂ = 6", x: 4.1, y: 0.7, tone: "ct", weight: 600 },
    {
      text: "(0,0)",
      x: 0,
      y: 0,
      tone: "ink",
      dx: -16,
      dy: 18,
      size: 12,
      weight: 600,
    },
    {
      text: "(4,0)",
      x: 4,
      y: 0,
      tone: "ink",
      dx: -16,
      dy: 18,
      size: 12,
      weight: 600,
    },
    {
      text: "(3,1)",
      x: 3,
      y: 1,
      tone: "ink",
      dx: 6,
      dy: -10,
      size: 12,
      weight: 600,
    },
    {
      text: "(0,2)",
      x: 0,
      y: 2,
      tone: "ink",
      dx: -36,
      dy: -5,
      size: 12,
      weight: 600,
    },
  ]}
>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    The feasible region is bounded by <span class="tone-s5">x₁ + x₂ ≤ 4</span>,
    <span class="tone-ct">x₁ + 3x₂ ≤ 6</span>, and the axes. Arrows mark the
    feasible side of each constraint line. The optimal vertex
    <span class="tone-pt">(3,1)</span> is where the 2 lines intersect.
  </Fragment>
</CartesianGraph>
